{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Why, etc.</b> Because HaShem is the supreme cause, which is the first, He said, \"Why do You lead us astray.\" Some answer that this is like the saying of our early Sages, \"It is not in their power to repent.\" Others say the verse speaks concerning thoughts. And some say, because we are in exile we cannot fulfill all the commandments that depend on the land." "<b>You harden.</b> Like the meaning of \"You remove,\" and similar to it, הקשיח בניה ללא לה (Job 39:16)." "<b>Return for the sake of Your servants.</b> They are the fathers, and \"for the sake of the tribes of Your heritage\" — they are the tribes."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:51.837742758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}